      "transcript": [
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "hi? someone told me to text this number about exercise stuff. what is zoh exactly? how does it work",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:40:00.000Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Hey, I'm ZOH, an AI coach the ZOH team built. I help you get better at one thing with a small step each day, and I check in by text to keep you on track. You can text \"stop\" anytime, and you can change how I coach just by telling me (\"chill out,\" \"push me harder\").\n\nExercise is a great place to start. What's your name, and what are you looking to work on?\n\n• Put AI to work for you\n• Read & learn more (books, ideas, any topic)\n• Start something on the side\n• Focus & get more done\n• Speak & connect better\n• Get fitter\n• Eat better\n• Sleep better\n• Learn a fun skill (Rubik's cube, card trick, play a song, drawing)\n• Not sure? Let's figure it out together",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:40:07.000Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "pat. i want to do something about exercise i guess. just walking maybe? i walk the dog sometimes lol",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:40:56.700Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Good to meet you, Pat. Walking is a great place to start, and the dog is built-in company. Tell me a bit about how those dog walks go now: where do you usually go, and how long are they?",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:41:03.700Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "we walk around the block mostly. maybe 10 min? not really sure what this is btw, is it like an app or a person",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:41:53.700Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Fair question, Pat. I'm an AI coach, not an app or a person. The ZOH team built me, and the founders read along to make me better. I text you a small step each day, you send a quick photo or screenshot as proof, and I keep you going.\n\nA 10 minute loop with the dog is a real start. What time of day could you walk them most days?",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:42:00.700Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "whenever",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:42:53.700Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Flexible is good, Pat, but a set time is what makes it stick. Which works better for you, right after work or after dinner?",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:43:00.700Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "the after work one i guess. what do u mean by proof tho, like take a pic of me walking??",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:43:23.100Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Not a pic of you, Pat. A quick photo works, like the dog's leash at the door or your street mid-walk. A screenshot from a step counter works too if you have one on your phone.\n\nGot it on after work. How many minutes can you give the walk on most days: 10, or a bit more?",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:43:30.100Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "Honestly not sure yet. Depends on the day. Maybe 30 min? Would that be too much to start",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:44:16.500Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Not too much, Pat. Walking 30 minutes is very doable, but you're at 10 now, and starting a little under what you can do helps it stick. I'd start at 15 minutes and let the good days run longer. Does 15 work for you?",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:44:23.500Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "the 15 min thing sounds ok. is that what i'd be doing every day then? or like some days off",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:45:09.900Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Up to you, Pat. Every day is fine, or you can take days off as long as it's at least 3 a week. Which days would you want to walk?",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:45:16.900Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "i dunno, prob most days. weekends prob too since the dog wants out lol. is it gonna send me reminders or do i have to remember",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:46:04.200Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Yes, I'll text you on your walk days to get you going, so you don't have to remember, Pat. I'll follow up if I haven't heard from you.\n\nWeekends are in. Which weekday do you want off: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday or Friday? Or would you rather just walk all seven?",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:46:11.200Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "i dunno, maybe no days off? just walk all 7. but wait, u said i could take some off? confusing lol",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:47:09.000Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Ha, sorry, that was confusing, Pat. Days off are optional. Seven days a week is a totally fine plan, so we'll go with all seven.\n\nOne last thing before I put it together: is there anything you'd like this walking to get you toward, like more energy or a longer walk? \"Not sure yet\" is a fine answer.",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:47:16.000Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "idk maybe just feel less wiped out after work? not sure yet tbh",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:48:05.400Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Feeling less wiped out after work is a great reason, Pat. Walking is a solid way to chase it. Here's the plan:\n\n• Headed for: feeling less wiped out after work\n• Day 1, today: 15-minute brisk-ish walk with the dog around the block\n• Every day at 5:30 pm, 15 minutes\n• Proof: a photo of the leash or your street mid-walk\n• Why: a short daily walk builds the habit, and it's a small enough step to keep up on tired days\n• Easy alternative: a step counter screenshot works too\n\nEach day shapes the next one. If 15 feels easy, we'll stretch it, always aiming at that after-work energy.\n\nWhat do you think?",
          "at": "2026-11-02T20:48:12.400Z"
        }
      ],
